        "original_id": "161c6482-a6c2-5e78-b8f9-9bb6b624170f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mark Rylance, Rudolf Abel, Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher, Alice Krige, Gottfried John\n- Works: Bridge of Spies, Institute Benjamenta\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, BAFTA Award for Best Supporting Actor\n- Roles: Soviet intelligence officer\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Ivanovich Abel, whose real name was Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher, was a Soviet intelligence officer who lived from July 11, 1903 to November 15, 1971.\n- In 2015, Mark Rylance portrayed Rudolf Abel in the film \"Bridge of Spies.\"\n- Mark Rylance won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his portrayal of Rudolf Abel in \"Bridge of Spies\" (2015).\n- Mark Rylance won the BAFTA Award for Best Supporting Actor for his portrayal of Rudolf Abel in \"Bridge of Spies\" (2015).\n- \"Institute Benjamenta\" stars Mark Rylance, Alice Krige, and Gottfried John.",
